---
title: "G2 Desktop and panels: ft-screens' screens and panels, when they show, ft-layout, floating windows, the dashboard, remote access over VNC (78e93b1, G2Desktop.tla)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    direction LR
    lg0: Off, hidden, or not started
    lg1: Shown, running, or arranged, as it should be
    lg2: Between: waiting for a pose, a viewer, the resume
    lg3: Hidden or stopped for a reason: the pause, conceal, the switch, a calibration
    lg4: Suspected open bug: the state that breaks the rule
    lg5: P1 open, ShownOnlyWanted: a desktop that starts with no head pose (headset off or asleep). apply_screens asks head before it sends anything (ft_layout.py 756), the caller only logs not arranged now (1955-1958, 2031-2038). No visibility, ingames, wrist, gesture, controllers or conceal reach ft-screens, so it keeps always and nothing concealed. Concealed screens show, toggle and dashboard users see them always, until a reset or a settings change (red P1.1-2, TLC HeadOff, 3 steps, HeadOffFix holds)
    lg6: P2 open, minor, ShownOnlyWanted: a full gaze calibration during a VR game with always and ingames hide. state gives g_mode (always), not the mode in effect (dashboard), so gazecheck.py 623 reads the screens as shown, and its show at close (1264-1265) turns the switch on under the dashboard mode. The screens stay over the game with the dashboard closed until it ends (red P2.1-2, TLC CalInGame, 5 steps, CalInGameFix holds)
    lg7: P3 open, minor, VncOffInPause: a desktop that starts mid-pause (autostart.sh on a SteamVR restart, the Desktop entry) runs remote-ctl.sh start with REMOTE=1 (frametop-session.sh 246-249) without a pause check. ft-screens hears pause on again, remote access doesn't stop. Same class as G1 L2 (red P3.1-2, TLC MidPause, 4 steps, MidPauseFix holds)
    lg8: Holds at 78e93b1: TypeOK in all 11 configs. All four rules in Fixed (932 states), FixedAlways (632), HeadOffFix, CalInGameFix, MidPauseFix. HiddenComesBack holds in the code configs: the switch, conceal and the pause come back while the programs run. VncComesBack holds everywhere
    lg9: Links, not new bugs: GazedCrash re-finds G4 Z1 (HiddenComesBack, 4 steps: ft-gazed dies mid-calibration, the hide stays). Lossy re-finds G1 L7 both ways: a lost pause off hides, a lost pause on shows through the pause, and only a new ft-screens hears it again. Crash-config liveness breaks count as noise
    lg10: Escape hatches: P1, Meta+Shift+R, the reset button, a settings change or a profile. P2, the hotkey, or the game ending (UpdateGame resets the switch). P3, Frametop Remote Access off, or pause and resume again
    lg11: Another group: arrows into it are where G2 touches it, drawn there, not here
  }
  class lg0 teal
  class lg1 blue
  class lg2 yellow
  class lg3 orange
  class lg4 breaks
  class lg5 bugLegend
  class lg6 bugLegend
  class lg7 bugLegend
  class lg8 fixed
  class lg9 legendNote
  class lg10 legendNote
  class lg11 xgroup
  state "Desktop start and stop (desktops.sh, frametop-session.sh 89-122, ft-layout start 1940-1968)" as ds {
    d0: Off: no ft-screens, no nested Plasma
    [*] --> d0
    d1: ft-screens up with its defaults: always, ingames hide, switch off, nothing concealed, not paused
    d2: Arranged: ft-layout placed the screens from the head and sent visibility, wrist, gesture, controllers, ingames, conceal and remote displays
    d3: Never sent: no head pose at the start, not arranged now, ft-screens keeps its defaults
    d4: Auto-arrange off: only the settings and the streams go, the screens stay where they were
  }
  state "One screen or panel shows when (UpdateVisibility 1236-1257, G2Desktop.tla Visible)" as sv {
    v0: Hidden: paused, concealed, the mode or the switch says no, a floating panel off or minimized
    [*] --> v0
    v1: Shown: not paused, not concealed, the mode says yes or it's being dragged
    v2: Pinned to a wrist: fades out past the wrist angle (60), pinned to the head: always in view
    v3: Shown against the settings: concealed but showing, or showing with the dashboard closed
  }
  state "The mode and the hide and show switch (ModeVisible 1177-1197, EffectiveMode 1162-1164)" as md {
    e0: always: shown unless the switch hides them
    [*] --> e0
    e1: dashboard: only with the SteamVR dashboard open, or the switch
    e2: toggle: only with the switch, gesture: looking at the controller, or the switch
    e3: always in a VR game with ingames hide: acts as dashboard
  }
  state "A full gaze calibration hides the screens (gazecheck.py 620-624, 1262-1266)" as cl {
    c0: No calibration
    [*] --> c0
    c1: Calibrating: read state (g_mode and the switch), saved shown, then hide
    c2: Closed: show again if it read them as shown
    c3: Shown over the game: the show turned the switch on under the dashboard mode in effect
  }
  state "The pause (game_pause.py 552-592, tell_screens 669-688, compositor.c schedule)" as pz {
    p0: Running
    [*] --> p0
    p1: Paused: pause on to ft-screens, everything hidden, relay buttons let go, ticks every 100 ms, remote access stopped if it ran
    p2: A desktop started mid-pause: the relay sends pause on again (screens_seen), remote access runs
  }
  state "ft-layout and the layout (ft_layout.py, layout.json, docs/profiles.md)" as ly {
    l0: layout.json: preset or custom, each screen's place, size, curve, pin and hidden, the visibility settings, remote displays
    l1: apply or reset: places every screen around the head, sends the settings, closes the VR keyboard
    l2: use PROFILE: its screens, hidden ones, remote displays and apps (ft-floatd profile)
    l3: hide N, show N (set_hidden): saved, and conceal or reveal now
  }
  state "Floating windows, drawn by hand (ft_floatd.py, frametop-float.js, docs/floating-windows.md)" as fw {
    f0: Docked: a window on a desktop screen in KWin
    f1: Floating: its own spare output WL-n and panel, cropped to the window, placed where it last floated
    f2: Minimized: the panel hides, the output stays
    f3: ft-floatd gone: started once by Plasma's autostart (frametop-session.sh 268-277), nothing restarts it
  }
  state "The dashboard and Steam's panels (steampanels.cpp, the gamepad pill)" as sp {
    s0: Dashboard closed
    [*] --> s0
    s1: Dashboard open: the dashboard mode shows the screens, near hand input on SteamVR's own panels, the gamepad pill over a screen
  }
  state "Remote access over the tailnet (remote-ctl.sh, remote-desktop.sh, vnc-bridge.sh, G2Desktop.tla vnc)" as vn {
    n0: Off: REMOTE=0, or no remote-capable file (the desktop started without it, exit 3)
    [*] --> n0
    n1: Waiting: krdp on 127.0.0.1 3390, Xvnc 20 on the tailnet address, port 5900, an 8-character VNC password
    n2: A viewer connected: FreeRDP from krdp into Xvnc, watch 15 to ft-screens every 5 s
    n3: Stopped by the pause: stopped remote, the resume starts it in a scope of its own
    n4: Running through the pause: the desktop started mid-pause
    n5: vnc-bridge gone: no tailscale0 address, or no remote-view for 90 s, nothing restarts it
  }
  state "How often ft-screens draws a screen (compositor.c frame_interval 704-718)" as fr {
    r0: Full rate: where you look, a video, typing on it, or a viewer watching (watch N, up to 60 s)
    r1: Lower for the rest of what you see
    r2: About once a second: hidden, behind you, or paused
  }
  state "Other groups" as og {
    o1: G1 Lifecycle and presence
    o3: G3 Input and pointer
    o4: G4 Gaze
    o5: G5 Hands
    o6: G6 Remote displays
  }
  d0 --> d1: desktops.sh start: autostart.sh when SteamVR starts, the dashboard's Desktop entry, a resume after a pause that closed it
  d1 --> d2: ft-layout start --wait 90 with a head pose
  d1 --> d3: (P1.1) the headset off or asleep: apply_screens asks head first (756) and raises, nothing is sent
  d3 --> v3: (P1.2) concealed screens show, toggle, gesture and dashboard users see them always
  d3 --> d2: Meta+Shift+R, the reset button, a settings change
  d1 --> d4: auto-arrange off: visibility and conceal still go (2007-2019)
  d2 --> d0: desktops.sh stop, SteamVR stops, ft-screens ends (Plasma ends with it)
  d1 --> p2: a new ft-screens while paused: pause on again
  d1 --> o1: G1: when the desktop starts and stops, L2
  d1 --> o5: G5: handsmode up starts hand tracking
  v0 --> v1: pause off, reveal, show, the mode says yes (the dashboard opens, a look at the controller)
  v1 --> v0: pause on, conceal, hide, the dashboard closes, a game in always with ingames hide
  v1 --> v2: pin to a wrist or the head
  v2 --> v1: unpin, or a reset
  v3 --> v0: a reset, or the escape hatches
  v1 --> r0: shown and looked at
  v0 --> r2: hidden
  e0 --> e3: a game starts, UpdateGame resets the switch
  e3 --> e0: the game ends, the switch reset again
  e0 --> e1: visibility from ft-layout, the switch reset
  e1 --> e2: visibility from ft-layout, the switch reset
  e3 --> v3: (P2.2) the calibration's show sets the switch on: shown with the dashboard closed
  e0 --> o3: G3: the screens_toggle key sends toggle
  c0 --> c1: a full calibration starts
  c1 --> c2: done or cancelled
  c2 --> c0: the switch back as it was, outside a game
  c1 --> c3: (P2.1) in a game, always with ingames hide: state says always 0, read as shown, hide changes nothing
  c3 --> c0: the game ends, or the hotkey
  c1 --> o4: G4 Z1: ft-gazed dies here, the hide stays
  p0 --> p1: a VR game (auto pause), pause_toggle
  p1 --> p0: resume: pause off, remote-ctl.sh start if it stopped it
  p1 --> o1: G1 L7: a lost pause off, g_paused sticks
  p1 --> p2: (P3.1) the desktop starts mid-pause: frametop-session.sh 246-249 starts remote access, no pause check
  p2 --> p0: resume: nothing marked stopped, remote access already running
  l0 --> l1: Meta+Shift+R, the reset button, Display Settings
  l0 --> l2: a profile:NAME key, Display Settings
  l0 --> l3: ft-layout hide N, show N, Display Settings
  l1 --> e0: visibility resets the switch
  l2 --> l1: then placed, or only send_hidden with no head pose (2076-2079)
  l3 --> v0: conceal
  l2 --> f1: ft-floatd moves or launches the profile's windows
  l1 --> o6: G6: start_remotes, place_remotes, conceal and reveal for remote displays
  f0 --> f1: the float key, the title-bar button, Launch as Standalone, a dashboard launch, a tear-off
  f1 --> f0: dock, carried onto a screen, the window closes
  f1 --> f2: minimized
  f2 --> f1: activate (frunner), unminimized
  f1 --> f3: ft-floatd dies
  f1 --> o3: G3: front N makes its window KWin's active one, typing focus
  o5 --> f1: G5: near input carries, stretches, throws and docks panels
  s0 --> s1: the dashboard opens
  s1 --> s0: it closes
  s1 --> e1: the dashboard mode shows the screens with it
  s1 --> o5: G5: hands work on SteamVR's panels
  n0 --> n1: the desktop starts with REMOTE=1, or Remote Access on in a capable desktop
  n1 --> n2: a VNC viewer connects
  n2 --> n1: the last viewer leaves, FreeRDP stops after 45 s
  n2 --> r0: watch 15: every screen at full rate
  n1 --> n3: a pause with running=1 (Xvnc and krdp both up)
  n3 --> n1: the resume
  n1 --> n0: the desktop stops (cleanup), Remote Access off
  n0 --> n4: (P3.2) the desktop starts mid-pause: remote access runs through the game
  n4 --> n1: the resume, which doesn't know it ran
  n1 --> n5: no tailnet address or layout
  n5 --> n1: Remote Access off and on, or a desktop restart
